#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/assets/df4f126da2ab3a0661bcb7dc18bb1e5eae8cd48d5c5a1464ea580ccc439195d6.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ 4s+4t=10 \\\\ 5s+6t=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ -4t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/assets/966d2d7cd1cd0ef04a1d9b2adc04511dea86cbbf254166988a7072e952879fe0.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb615b07-46fa-5c9b-bd12-0e4983282da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321585} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee33ddf-b597-56c5-a884-20d5c9cabffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321586} {:answer/id #uuid "14ed59de-3ac0-5711-9017-c18c6857811b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321587} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4ff864-903f-56ea-9b99-e95f93374b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321588} {:answer/id #uuid "a988dae2-4651-5294-a8e4-88f9fa56f040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14ed59de-3ac0-5711-9017-c18c6857811b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321587} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb72595-3a95-5b00-ba54-0bcdfa25110c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6dd9a94f-9ad6-5f46-b62e-569214d55f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105208" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=9\\cdot (-2)=-18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016f2f8c-fd18-5e2f-ad49-8b63df7ea0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321592} {:answer/id #uuid "52ae24db-da19-54f0-85da-d399e1221047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321593} {:answer/id #uuid "d492b328-12ec-5465-8bbc-79f6d2874d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321594} {:answer/id #uuid "5220edbc-b5c0-58c8-9b69-dcfea2e6d242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321595} {:answer/id #uuid "6580d99c-acbc-583d-86e7-e4ffb400bd0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52ae24db-da19-54f0-85da-d399e1221047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321593} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f29a00-9ddc-5699-a576-55ea4802d9ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d568260-07d9-5911-8f12-d84f51b62506" :question/math-academy-id "q-105232" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+8.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+8\\,⇒\\,k=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021830cc-4042-5729-a832-bf1a1619ca6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321599} {:answer/id #uuid "e5860fe3-9e53-5844-8da4-5626f6c80d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321600} {:answer/id #uuid "438e232a-96bd-55c4-add7-01c09510659b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321601} {:answer/id #uuid "37eef5c8-54b7-59ed-8fc8-eaf24aeb72d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321602} {:answer/id #uuid "e527053a-7bd9-5f9a-8f62-e1f6a858bea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021830cc-4042-5729-a832-bf1a1619ca6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321599} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7e32541-a65b-59d6-b00e-ba055641c9c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "559d0955-6d85-5796-be86-804131223c74" :question/math-academy-id "q-105237" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86083343-f5dc-5358-8bdb-bed4acc7f607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321606} {:answer/id #uuid "ba40a497-bd29-5a8a-88c5-da3be2fc3127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321607} {:answer/id #uuid "7e37625e-67e1-579a-96c0-bf1239ecc3e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321608} {:answer/id #uuid "443df4b5-e4b5-54e0-8e07-13a15dcf90db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321609} {:answer/id #uuid "69ac4cab-1188-5e5c-b31d-514da01b0a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86083343-f5dc-5358-8bdb-bed4acc7f607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321606} :answer-field/id #uuid "825ac608-b8f0-51ed-a171-30cf2a1bec19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1fa0e2a6-610a-53f4-8250-0d5b9843d7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-105257" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$, $c=⟨-4,5,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,1,4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-4t=1 \\\\ -2s+5t=1 \\\\ -s-t=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-4t=1 \\\\ t=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25591cd3-a808-5cc3-b9ed-561f523bbb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321613} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbd4e43-db7f-564c-abce-1e83b1ffa41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321614} {:answer/id #uuid "7710f546-b2e7-567e-a45b-c3c3967465fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321615} {:answer/id #uuid "5702ee51-6cef-58d2-a0bc-5c96272a1946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321616} {:answer/id #uuid "f8daea0e-c64e-58c2-922a-2e216a8d4f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbd4e43-db7f-564c-abce-1e83b1ffa41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321614} :answer-field/id #uuid "c98ae834-d6e5-5e94-95ff-d0c5693e27f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b66462e-04c5-5d86-b74a-2babd3618089" :question/math-academy-id "q-105265" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,-1,4⟩$, $c=⟨-3,-8,14⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-10,-14⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ -s-8t=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ t=3 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-14b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea4c1454-1b3f-5538-848a-5fd619152623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321620} {:answer/id #uuid "94c7eda6-95b2-5699-9ecb-21fc7eedb7a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321621} {:answer/id #uuid "de4e7fc1-1202-5824-8901-d6141ce31e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321622} {:answer/id #uuid "03c059cb-ba7a-56c2-b295-31bf1e79c393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321623} {:answer/id #uuid "d97435db-465c-5813-92b0-2de72eb9fdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97435db-465c-5813-92b0-2de72eb9fdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321624} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4802b34-38f1-5390-8fff-a8dca2a5666e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfb9b107-bb38-574d-9d31-74a75b24630d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34115" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f204524e-4116-501e-83c4-be141bd29db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321626} {:answer/id #uuid "ea49568e-d765-5a6e-be64-9de73076c2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321627} {:answer/id #uuid "69cbe801-d1f0-5ca9-872d-1d42ec604929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321628} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb2b449-5d97-5452-b918-515a32282b6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321629} {:answer/id #uuid "1437f229-0745-5b73-bb04-2f33d5846286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1437f229-0745-5b73-bb04-2f33d5846286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321630} :answer-field/id #uuid "8af14708-1e6f-5969-bc5a-1b1d6f0a0eb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d12a13d-137e-5159-9c9a-8fb99c09543c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34205" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-2)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b58a776-0241-50c0-b9f5-4f9480215e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117935} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3cfd2f-178e-5550-959f-81ed64858f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117936} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c201c5-1423-508e-8535-384e618ed30b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117937} {:answer/id #uuid "1816acc5-0964-5cf2-9219-a97227a8faa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117938} {:answer/id #uuid "4e2e4b88-69f4-5630-9ef7-89a8da40a766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce3cfd2f-178e-5550-959f-81ed64858f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117936} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ecbaffe-cf4e-5822-809e-5c0fd608abf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3767254e-f5e7-559c-aca3-b6417b0458c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34211" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,5⟩$, $c=⟨1,-5,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-8,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ 3s-5t=-8 \\\\ 5s-7t=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ -2t=-5 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+\\frac{5}{2} & =1 \\\\ -s & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{3}{2},\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{3}{2}b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{15}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9038653-6dfc-5338-a1d2-4cd3f8208042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321632} {:answer/id #uuid "6741c7be-efc6-5c87-a5b6-8fd597131011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321633} {:answer/id #uuid "286b3bfd-bb1e-55da-b63e-1e2bc61e4cc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321634} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec1f383-9f9e-5904-a363-bb829c7e4293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321635} {:answer/id #uuid "621bbf6e-3f85-5bc3-951c-b5a05ad74add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ec1f383-9f9e-5904-a363-bb829c7e4293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321635} :answer-field/id #uuid "194dafa2-2b03-5c39-a290-c859fc81bf99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46516d2-c8a1-53ed-ad0e-7623ea65bae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34635" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=12,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55d979c5-d8c3-5d45-9a13-3bde977c2303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321639} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ec153e-dc90-5cd6-a9cd-dceca4c18587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321640} {:answer/id #uuid "c94e43bb-d328-5fa3-8629-ea2d3a2c9768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321641} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2a3e2a-0442-57b8-9373-51c89185b4fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321642} {:answer/id #uuid "a8537e0a-becc-57ba-bc94-0de8c73a7c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55d979c5-d8c3-5d45-9a13-3bde977c2303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321639} :answer-field/id #uuid "09dd38cc-9e8f-5783-b409-60d5fcdf2024" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54622a3c-c837-5839-bfc6-04c5108dd79e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74546" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=8\\cdot (-2)=-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5143d008-c998-5ca6-8a3a-26ae992831ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321646} {:answer/id #uuid "10ae71dd-d5ef-5bd7-896b-ea709d479c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321647} {:answer/id #uuid "6df89077-db62-5002-a7c6-0b199db968e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321648} {:answer/id #uuid "99bf9e33-d26e-5746-a850-3ea474888432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321649} {:answer/id #uuid "89556f1a-7181-5388-bd0c-060913686783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5143d008-c998-5ca6-8a3a-26ae992831ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321646} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb7e360-7575-5b7e-8821-7c42c3c00bae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5f41c33-ba44-553c-9d8e-b9b2487dc872" :question/math-academy-id "q-74556" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ea69e9e-ef6e-58af-9567-fc94965e2d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321653} {:answer/id #uuid "956e72df-0a8a-5b09-bebe-c61dbb88da6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321654} {:answer/id #uuid "07417ab2-0b75-5c31-bf01-d9061a7be69a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321655} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad3cd87-5477-5334-81e0-04690e43995e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321656} {:answer/id #uuid "07aa8e8f-2c7d-596c-9242-f1c9dcea3eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ad3cd87-5477-5334-81e0-04690e43995e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321656} :answer-field/id #uuid "9234abd0-1fd1-565b-9e3c-169693804108" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c8c0bca-8eb9-5923-818b-c8e90bfe8436" :question/math-academy-id "q-74557" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 7 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k+12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c7657ec-ac76-5b07-8598-592ea6d0ace7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321660} {:answer/id #uuid "b006b8fd-c45b-5589-9c90-c1f27c3b0b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321661} {:answer/id #uuid "365ed788-6488-5d7b-81f6-ce2ba9dd147d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321662} {:answer/id #uuid "5a47cd1a-fc7a-5945-a971-b721c35d840f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321663} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba0dc4c-6d61-5420-9e8b-f982af0a06b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b006b8fd-c45b-5589-9c90-c1f27c3b0b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321661} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8b883f0-e59d-57f2-83e1-91e80eb69e23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b86270f7-83e5-5a5f-ba86-e643f0a0d4f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74596" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+45\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+45.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+45\\,⟹\\,k=-45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "652a9716-b89e-52a2-85ba-011e3168e304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321667} {:answer/id #uuid "92ce38a3-ec05-5b48-bcb7-12b3ce4388ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321668} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc630ac-78b1-5b28-b5ed-de0857aca0ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321669} {:answer/id #uuid "b6aae522-4b3f-539a-a749-9df91068b71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321670} {:answer/id #uuid "31362ee6-5927-5a81-93f3-21b21b5a3535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "652a9716-b89e-52a2-85ba-011e3168e304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321667} :answer-field/id #uuid "58a94fa7-ae30-5bc9-8f07-4a3652330594" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46351b92-d9f0-569c-9f65-f2e2b36c50d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74599" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨1,-6,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-10,-15⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ 4s-6t=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t=-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ -2t=-6 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8e09920-9bdb-5ee8-9ffd-fd14db071b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321674} {:answer/id #uuid "a9030de0-c720-58c1-8888-ffe72dc673d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321675} {:answer/id #uuid "15d3c38d-25ee-5522-8598-916d4f036c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321676} {:answer/id #uuid "5e63632b-8c0e-5df2-beed-ea018b56869d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321677} {:answer/id #uuid "3be89d01-b4f4-56d8-8d78-3b80c74b9887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e63632b-8c0e-5df2-beed-ea018b56869d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321677} :answer-field/id #uuid "1091e923-9213-5fb8-9cfb-5e6ee791ac88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f2e2ca9-f3dd-52d9-9085-3a8a08fb33a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74605" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,3,6⟩$, $c=⟨1,-2,4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,19,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 19 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+t=3 \\\\ 3s-2t=19 \\\\ 6s+4t=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 19 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -32\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-32,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}]}
